2026-09-02T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2177) 'description: When tagging an RFD's altitude, use the flight_level field on its serial-register entry. Values are L1 (operations, single-team execution), L2 (coordination, cross-team value flow), L3 (strategy, portfolio bet). Follow Klaus Leopold's numbering (L1 = ground, L3 = altitude). Tagging is opt-in.
 # tags: rfd:front-matter
 Text:RFD2177  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-02T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2177) 'tools: Read, Edit
 # tags: rfd:front-matter
 Text:RFD2177  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-02T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2177) '---
 # tags: rfd:front-matter
 Text:RFD2177  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-02T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2177) 'Tag an RFD's altitude and find all the strategy decisions at once.
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2177  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-02T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2177) 'A reader wanting "all the strategy decisions" must read every RFD and infer each altitude, because the register carries no field for it.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2177  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-02T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2177) 'Run `scripts/render_flight_level_pages.py` after you add a `flight_level` tag, then check the RFD appears on its per-level page. The sections below hold the tag schema and the citation.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2177  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-02T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-2177) 'flight levels taxonomy
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2177  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-02T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-2177) 'Every RFD carries an optional `flight_level` tag, L1/L2/L3 (Flight Levels: execution / coordination / strategy), and three Quarto listings render from that tag; tagging is opt-in.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2177  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-02T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-2177) 'RFD66606-1000 (RFD conventions), RFD66606-1053 (OpenUSD internal format), RFD66606-2174 (open-abandoned index) and RFD66606-2176 (committed-terminal index): same pattern of one document plus tag.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2177  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-02T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-2177) 'Levels and rendering
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2177  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-02T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-2177) '  L1  Operations    how a single team executes; fast cadence L2  Coordination  how work flows across teams to deliver value L3  Strategy      portfolio decisions about where to invest
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2177  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-02T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-2177) 'Numbering follows Klaus Leopold's original: L1 is ground, L3 is altitude, matching the flight-altitude metaphor. The register is greenfield for this axis, so no earlier convention needs inverting.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2177  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-02T00:00:17Z (RFD66606-2177) '`scripts/render_flight_level_pages.py` reads the tag from every serial register and writes three Quarto listings under `pages/flight-level-{1,2,3}-*.qmd`. Navbar carries a Flight Levels dropdown. Untagged RFDs stay off the three pages.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2177  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-02T00:00:18Z (RFD66606-2177) 'See DETAILS.md for the tag schema, the render script's shape, and the Klaus Leopold citation.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2177  1 LINE
 Text:Written

